  "problem_statement": "iter_find_files: max_depth parameter missing\n\nI was trying to use the iter_find_files function with the max_depth parameter to limit how deep it searches in subdirectories, but it seems like the parameter is missing.\n\n```python\nfrom boltons.fileutils import iter_find_files\n\n# This works\nfiles = list(iter_find_files(\"my_directory\", patterns=[\"*.py\"]))\n\n# This fails\nfiles = list(iter_find_files(\"my_directory\", patterns=[\"*.py\"], max_depth=1))\n# TypeError: iter_find_files() got an unexpected keyword argument 'max_depth'\n```\n\nThe documentation mentions the max_depth parameter, but when I try to use it, I get an error saying it's an unexpected keyword argument."
